    "show_share": true,
    "description": "For the first time in Pakistan, radiologists at the Aga Khan University Hospital successfully have treated a bone tumour (non-cancerous) without surgery using a procedure called radiofrequency ablation (RFA). The procedure was performed on 24-year-old Bilal in May and follow-up visits confirm that the patient's symptoms have completely disappeared.",
